\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Gas fraction within $500c$ versus halo mass, for the 16--84\% band, median, and strongest-feedback (2.5\%) edge of the 256-node Sobol design, compared to the mainstream X-ray relation of \citet  {eckert19} and the eROSITA strong-feedback edge of \citet  {popesso24}, over $M_{500c}=10^{13}$--$3\times 10^{14}\,{\rm  M}_\odot /h$. The horizontal dashed line marks the cosmic baryon fraction $\Omega _b/\Omega _m$. Takeaway: \emph  {no} point in the 30-dimensional TNG-like feedback prior -- including its most extreme feedback tail -- reaches the eROSITA band; the entire Sobol volume sits above the strong-feedback curve.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:erosita}{{3}{7}{Gas fraction within $500c$ versus halo mass, for the 16--84\% band, median, and strongest-feedback (2.5\%) edge of the 256-node Sobol design, compared to the mainstream X-ray relation of \citet {eckert19} and the eROSITA strong-feedback edge of \citet {popesso24}, over $\Mfive =10^{13}$--$3\times 10^{14}\,\Msun /h$. The horizontal dashed line marks the cosmic baryon fraction $\Omega _b/\Omega _m$. Takeaway: \emph {no} point in the 30-dimensional TNG-like feedback prior -- including its most extreme feedback tail -- reaches the eROSITA band; the entire Sobol volume sits above the strong-feedback curve}{figure.3}{}}
