\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Ray-traced BIND shear$\times y$ cross-correlation $\xi _{\gamma y}(\theta )$ (16--84\% Sobol band, $2.4'$-beam-convolved solid, no-beam dotted) compared to the real DES Y3$\times $ACT measurement \citep  {gatti22,pandey22} for DES source bins 3 and 4. The shaded regions outside the robust $8'$--$40'$ window are affected by the finite ($5^\circ $) field low-$\ell $ cut. Takeaway: at robust scales, BIND is $\approx 2.5\times $/$2.3\times $ above the real data in bins 3/4 -- confirming, at the field level and against real survey data, the same gas-excess tension identified per-halo in Section~\ref {sec:results3}. (The panel's own super-title rounds this to a stale ``$\sim 1.5$--$2\times $'' estimate from an earlier reduction pass; the precise, current values are the in-panel-annotated and body-text $2.5\times $/$2.3\times $ quoted here.)}}{15}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:field_desy3}{{10}{15}{Ray-traced BIND shear$\times y$ cross-correlation $\xi _{\gamma y}(\theta )$ (16--84\% Sobol band, $2.4'$-beam-convolved solid, no-beam dotted) compared to the real DES Y3$\times $ACT measurement \citep {gatti22,pandey22} for DES source bins 3 and 4. The shaded regions outside the robust $8'$--$40'$ window are affected by the finite ($5^\circ $) field low-$\ell $ cut. Takeaway: at robust scales, BIND is $\approx 2.5\times $/$2.3\times $ above the real data in bins 3/4 -- confirming, at the field level and against real survey data, the same gas-excess tension identified per-halo in Section~\ref {sec:results3}. (The panel's own super-title rounds this to a stale ``$\sim 1.5$--$2\times $'' estimate from an earlier reduction pass; the precise, current values are the in-panel-annotated and body-text $2.5\times $/$2.3\times $ quoted here.)}{figure.10}{}}
